orm using props for submission URL), Dashboard (placeholder “Document List coming soon”).\\\\n\\\\n5. TypeScript & Linting\\\\n   • Strict mode ON.  No eslint / ts errors.\\\\n\\\\n6. Build Assumption\\\\n   • Vite base=\\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\".\\\\n\\\\nReturn the complete, compilable src/App.tsx as the body of your REPORT for uiux_task_v1. No other files. Use TODO comments where implementation by other teams is pending.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 6,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"uiux_task_v1\\\"\\n}\\n###order_uiux_v1###\\n\\n###order_cms_v1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Supervisor_CMS (Tagge – ID 5)\\\\nSequence ID: cms_task_v1\\\\n\\\\nDeliverable (single file): lambda/index.ts  (Node 18 Lambda handler)\\\\n\\\\nScope & Requirements\\\\n1. Trigger & Inputs\\\\n   • Event: S3 ObjectCreated in bucket dunbaroakshoa-site-${ACCOUNT_ID}, prefix /news-source/.\\\\n   • New object is a markdown file named YYYY-MM-DD-slug.md.\\\\n\\\\n2. Processing Logic\\\\n   • List all objects under /news-source/.\\\\n   • For each, read markdown; convert to HTML using unified + remark-parse + remark-html.\\\\n   • Output: write HTML to key /news/YYYY/MM/DD/slug/index.html  (based on filename date & slug).\\\\n   • Update /news/feed.json (Array of posts [{title, url, date}…]).\\\\n\\\\n3. CloudFront Cache Busting\\\\n   • After writes, call createInvalidation via AWS SDK v3 for paths /news/*.\\\\n\\\\n4. Error Handling & Idempotency\\\\n   • Retry safe; handle duplicate filenames gracefully.\\\\n\\\\n5. Unit Tests (inline Jest)\\\\n   • Include at least one Jest test (in same file under /** jest tests **/) that mocks S3 + CloudFront, validates conversion.\\\\n\\\\n6. Performance Limits\\\\n   • Memory 128 MB, timeout 30 s; process ≤100 posts per run.\\\\n\\\\nReturn complete lambda/index.ts (including imports) as the body of your REPORT for cms_task_v1. No extra files.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 5,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"cms_task_v1\\\"\\n}\\n###order_cms_v1###\\n\\n###order_cicd_v1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Supervisor_CICD (T – ID 4)\\\\nSequence ID: cicd_task_v1\\\\n\\\\nDeliverable (single file): lib/frontend-stack.ts  (AWS CDK v2 TypeScript stack)\\\\n\\\\nScope & Requirements\\\\n1. Stack Name: FrontendStack\\\\n2. Resources\\\\n   a. S3 Bucket dunbaroakshoa-site-${Account} with websiteHosting (index.html) and blocked public ACL; originAccessControl for CloudFront.\\\\n   b. ACM Cert (us-east-1) for dunbaroakshoa.com & www.dunbaroakshoa.com with DNS validation.\\\\n   c. CloudFront Distribution\\\\n      • Origin = bucket via OAC\\\\n      • DefaultRootObject index.html; 403/404 → /index.html\\\\n      • Behaviours: /documents/* (Origin same, cache disabled, requireSignedCookie = true), default = public\\\\n   d. Route 53 Hosted Zone & A/AAAA alias records to distribution (root & www).\\\\n   e. CloudFront Function ‘authCookieSetter’ (placeholder inline function code string setting cookies from query params id_token etc.). Attach to /auth/callback.\\\\n   f. Lambda ‘news-builder’ (code from lambda/index.ts asset) with ObjectCreated trigger on /news-source/.\\\\n   g. CodeCommit Repository ‘hoa-frontend’.\\\\n   h. CodeBuild project (standard Linux 2 image, commands: npm ci && npm run build).\\\\n   i. CodePipeline (Source → Build → Deploy) – deploy stage runs aws s3 sync and CloudFront invalidation via buildspec.\\\\n3. Outputs\\\\n   • SiteURL (https://dunbaroakshoa.com)\\\\n   • BucketName, DistributionId.\\\\n4. Determinism\\\\n   • Use hard-coded logical IDs or consistent ID generation (e.g., `${id}-bucket`).\\\\n5. No extraneous constructs; compile with ts-node.\\\\n\\\\nReturn full lib/frontend-stack.ts as the body of your REPORT for cicd_task_v1. No additional files.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 4,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"cicd_task_v1\\\"\\n}\\n###order_cicd_v1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_